[[Qaysanic Burawa]] was a period in Kaftian history between 2rd century and 7th century AD where [[Burawa]] was divided between four kingdoms and 12 city states that lay on the Burawi coast. The coast of Burawa had mainly been under the control of trading cities and the coastal [[Kingdom of Iskhal]] while the interior had been governed by three primarily inland kingdoms, the [[Kingdom of Ufyen]], the [[Kingdom of Iracwi]] and the [[Kingdom of Sago]]. The Qaysanic period would see its decline starting 403, when the [[Kingdom of Burawa]] had formed to unite the coastal city states and eventually conquer the three kingdoms during the [[Northern Conquest of Burawa]]